{
  "$comment": "The shelves RPM files records under, and the styles that hang off them. Single source: RPM.Core/Metadata/Subgenres.cs and Genres.All are generated from this by scripts/gen_subgenres.py and are never hand-edited. Order is the order things are offered in, so it is deliberate. A style is a name, or {\"name\", \"styles\"} for a main style with the styles under it, nested as deep as needed; the picker shows the styles under a main style indented beneath it, and the nesting never decides a shelf. A name under more than one shelf is offered under each and is matched to none of them, because a style belonging to three shelves names no one of them. 'blocked' are words that fall out of splitting a tag and must never be read as a style; they bind the style lookup only, and several are perfectly good shelf words. A blocked word that folds onto a real style costs that style its key: it is still offered in the picker and is not matched out of a tag, which is what 'alternative & punk' does to Alternative Punk and is deliberate.",
